WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:06.359
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and since Arrow
and the Flash have continued to cast new comic

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:10.120
book characters I wanted to do a villains
power ranking. This will just be for Arrow

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:15.230
Season 3. I might do a version of this for
the Flash in the next week or two.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.300
The newest villain is Komodo, he’s going
to be played by Matt Ward. You may remember

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.939
him from Tron Legacy. He was cast as Simon
Lacroix, but in the comics Lacroix is Komodo,

00:00:23.939 --> 00:00:25.890
that’s why we say Matt Ward is playing Komodo.
The same is also true for all the other actors.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:26.210
Usually when they cast someone, they list
them under their alter ego.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.800
Think of it in terms of Batman, Bruce Wayne
is the fake identity. Batman is who he really

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.619
is inside, The Dark Knight. So his name Bruce
Wayne, is his alter ego.

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:36.620
Arrow season 3 will refer to pretty much all
of these villains by their real life personas.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.010
With the exception of Ra’s Al Ghul. He has
no alter ego, unless you want to consider

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:44.520
the Demon’s Head. He’s really the same
person no matter who he’s talking too though,

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.129
there’s no secret identity.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:50.820
This list is going to be least powerful to
most powerful starting with Manhunter.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.590
This is the Mark Shaw Manhunter, Not Martian
Manhunter. The one who’s associated with

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.370
the Suicide Squad in the comics. He’s going
to be part of a Diggle Amanda Waller story,

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.530
so I’m guessing he’s not a flashback character.
Remember, some of the people they’ve cast

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.630
are only going to appear in the Hong Kong
Flashbacks and some will only appear in present

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:07.780
day.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:10.270
Most people associated with Arrow’s version
of the Suicide Squad are hitmen and mercenaries

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:10.930
who for some reason landed on Amanda Waller’s
shit list.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:14.390
For those that have read the comics, the most
recent version of Manhunter is Kate Spencer,

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.860
which gives me some interesting theories for
Laurel.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:22.570
Mark Shaw was originally a public defender
who later was trained by a secret society

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:26.310
called the Manhunters. He joined so that he
could serve justice to criminals in a more

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:31.070
effective way. Like Frank Castle becoming
the Punisher. And just like the Punisher,

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:38.070
Shaw eventually went a little nuts and started
going way over the line. Effectively becoming

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.140
a villain.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:44.829
This is a really interesting point, yes you
can be a villain even if you’re not trying

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:50.710
to be evil. Think of Shaw as a hero that wandered
off the path. Which is probably how Arrow

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.780
is going to treat him. Usually doing something
like that will put you in an ARGUS jail cell.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.119
He was a part of the older Suicide Squad comics,
but like I said. On the show, he’ll just

00:01:58.119 --> 00:01:59.070
be butting heads with Diggle.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:04.430
In the new 52 comics, the reboot. Mark Shaw
is a US Marshall. Still has questionable morality.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:08.570
I’m kind of curious to see if Arrow does
that mix and match thing where they give Laurel

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:15.570
some aspects of the Kate Spencer Manhunter
blended with Shaw’s hunter in the old comics.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:24.430
Like Laurel works at the DAs office, she’s
going to be training to fight this season,

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:29.010
either with Wildcat or Oliver, probably both.
So what if they have an episode where she

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:34.440
tries to dispense her own personal justice.
Kind of combining the original Mark Shaw manhunter

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:41.440
with the Kate Spencer manhunter. Kate Spencer
was a Federal Prosecutor in the comics.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:52.020
I’m not expecting it, but keep your eyes
peeled for non-black canary Laurel kicking

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:53.770
some butt.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:57.680
Increasing the threat level a little, next
is Thea Queen. I’m not going to call her

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.020
Artemis, but I think the show is pushing her
in that direction. I know a lot of you want

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:07.170
her to be Lady Shiva, but think more of Artemis
in Young Justice. Only as more an antagonist

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.440
to Team Arrow.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:14.590
Willa Holland and Colton Haynes actually posted
this picture from the set. You can see the

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:19.630
new short haircut she’s sporting and she’s
also posted pictures from the gym. The show

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.760
is still pairing her with Roy but since she’s
on Team Merlyn this year that technically

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.730
makes her a villain.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:30.230
I know a lot of you might not totally be convinced
Thea could ever be a threat to Roy but remember,

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:35.530
she was a champion Archer and Merlyn has the
wisdom of the League of Assassins to use when

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:40.360
he trains her. Oliver had Slade, so I wouldn’t
call one better than the other. But right

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:47.360
now I think 
Merlyn is a better teacher than Oliver is.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:05.400
Part of the fun this season will be watching
Oliver train Roy more and watching Merlyn

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:06.820
train Thea.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:12.000
Then it will really get fun when Thea starts
kicking Roy’s butt.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.000
Climbing the ladder a little further is Deadshot,
Michael Rowe is guest starring in the Suicide

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.790
Squad related episodes. I’m expecting to
see him more than once. There’s going to

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:26.120
at least be one special Suicide Squad episode.
But they get cameos in other episodes. Expect

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.090
him to get a really cool story.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:31.420
Speaking of which, I didn’t put her on the
list but Harley Quinn is supposed to have

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:38.420
a real cameo this season. Like an actual one
that makes it to air. When Cassidy Alexa did

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:43.320
her last season, they had the super short
teaser that got cut out of the Suicide Squad

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:50.320
episode. Then she had another cameo in the
finale that also got cut out at the last minute.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.640
Stephen Amell was pretty vocal about wanting
to see her on the show a couple of months

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:59.570
ago. They probably won’t make any special
annoucements till we get closer. But be prepared

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:05.270
for Harley Quinn.
Just above Deadshot I’m putting Komodo.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:09.540
He was a huge Green Arrow Villain in the new
52 comics. He was connected to Oliver’s

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:13.850
father and even worked inside Queen Industries.
I don’t know how the show is going to change

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:20.850
him from the comics, but he could potentially
show up in the flashbacks and in present day.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:28.400
In present day he’ll be connected to Count
Vertigo. There was a comic book plot where

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:32.710
he kidnapped Shado’s daughter and helped
Vertigo so he might end up kidnapping or trying

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:34.620
to kidnap Felicity or Laurel.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:41.620
Since Laurel’s going to be training if she
does end up fighting Komodo it would be a

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.030
pretty cool takedown for her. They’d have
to de-power him a little from his comic book

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:50.600
version. He’s supposed to be Oliver’s
equal and I don’t see Laurel becoming as

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.290
good a fighter as Oliver right away.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:59.500
Next step up we’re getting into supervillain
territory. There’s Talia Al Ghul. She is

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:03.300
coming back as part of the Ra’s Al Ghul,
League of Assassins episodes. Or the episodes

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.950
that feature the League.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:09.370
Black Canary is only back for three episodes,
so I’m expecting Talia to show up sometime

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:10.220
during those.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:15.210
In terms of fighting ability she’s right
under Oliver. She was able to fight him to

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:20.460
a stand still last season in hand to hand
combat and with a bow. But Oliver is still

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.690
stronger just from sheer size.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.060
Some of these upper level characters are better
than each other under certain conditions,

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:32.370
like Talia is more vicious than Oliver or
Merlyn for instance, but both of them are

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:36.389
stronger. A lot of times it just depends on
the conditions of the fight and whether or

00:06:36.389 --> 00:06:36.880
not one of them is confounded.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:42.320
But moving up to my top 3. Amanda Waller.
Yes, I am considering her a villain. She’s

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:46.740
neutral really, but the way Arrow uses her
is mostly as an antagonist. She only helps

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:51.460
Team Arrow when she’s forced to or when
it suits her. If you’re even a little bit

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:56.280
evil, you’re a villain. Villains can still
do good things and continue to be villains.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:56.919
Just like Merlyn.

00:06:56.919 --> 00:07:01.570
I think Waller will be way more evil in the
Hong Kong flashbacks. She’s clearly keeping

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:04.580
Oliver there against his wishes forcing him
to help her.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:10.090
I know everyone is wondering how he ended
back on the island in the pilot, if that supposedly

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:14.360
came after Hong Kong. It’s probably because
he and Waller had a falling out. I’m hoping

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:18.389
that the flashbacks this season explain why.

00:07:18.389 --> 00:07:22.980
Up to number 2 now, Malcolm Merlyn. Who is
nothing like John Barrowman in real life.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:26.860
Stephen Amell said that the biggest prankster
on set is John Barrowman. Like the kind of

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:27.860
person who will jump from around the corner
with jazz hands to scare you.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:31.370
I love the thought that Malcolm Merlyn is
a consummate prankster. Like the Tom Hiddleston

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:35.030
Loki of the series. Meaning that even if he
does evil things, he’s really true neutral.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:42.030
As in he can either swing chaotic neutral
or lawful neutral depending on the situation.

00:07:43.389 --> 00:07:50.389
I’m wondering if he’s going to try and
play Team Arrow against Ra’s Al Ghul. Like

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:55.570
use them as a distraction. Or better yet.
Use Team Arrow as a Human Shield.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:08:01.240
It’s also totally possible that Merlyn and
Oliver could team up while still being enemies.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:08.240
Like a temporary truce to fight off Ra’s
Al Ghul.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:13.840
Stephen Amell said that Oliver and Merlyn
will always have unfinished business, mostly

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:17.830
referring to Tommy and the Earth Shaker. But
Ra’s Al Ghul is the one thing that could

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.699
put that fight on hold.

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:26.010
Let me know if you want to one, see Oliver
and Merlyn go at it and two, do you want to

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:28.889
see them team up against Ra’s Al Ghul?

00:08:28.889 --> 00:08:32.860
Which of course leads me to the most powerful
villain this season, The Demon’s Head.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:36.250
The big thing with him this season is what
is compelling enough for him to leave Nanda

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:42.800
Parbat and come to Starling? Usually what
you see is all the villains stories tie together

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:47.310
by the end. So Ra’s Al Ghul will be in Starling
because of something Black Canary does, something

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.970
Merlyn does and something Vertigo does.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:54.410
That doesn’t include any interaction between
Ray Palmer’s story or any of the other heroes

00:08:54.410 --> 00:09:01.410
coming on the show. I’ll try to address
that when I do a Hero Power Ranking, be sure

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:11.680
to subscribe to get that video. I’ll post
it next week.

